fficial\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9597) - AMD Ryzen 7 5700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.94 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using a spatial shader that sets POINT_SIZE and accesses UV, meshes that contain vertex color data trigger a rendering validation error:\n\n```\nE 0:00:02:112   draw_list_draw: Number of instances requested (70218 is larger than the maximum number supported by the bound vertex array (70217).\n<C++ Error>   Condition \"p_instances > draw_list.validation.vertex_max_instances_allowed\" is true.\n<C++ Source>  servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp:5007 @ draw_list_draw()\n```\n\nKey observations:\n\n- Happens only in Forward+ and Mobile renderer\n- Happens only when the mesh has vertex color data\n- Happens when a shader:\n  - sets POINT_SIZE\n  - references UV (even if just reading it)\n- The error is consistently off-by-one:\n  - instances requested = vertex count\n  - max allowed = vertex count - 1\n- Reproducible with:\n  - Primitive meshes (cube, sphere, etc.)\n  - Meshes modified via MeshDataTool or ArrayMesh\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the attached minimal reproduction project\n2. Ensure rendering method is Forward+\n3. In the main scene enable the node cube_v_color (cube with vertex colors)\n5. Run the scene\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nhttps://github.com/disibaro/bug-test","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"h